# Dreadhorde Arcanist's "If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead" is a replacement effect (CR
# 614.1a), ordered by the spell's controller with the others that would change the same move (CR 616.1). Faithless Looting
# on turn 1 discards a Lightning Bolt and a Lightning Strike; Bot2 has Dauthi Voidwalker ("If a card would be put into an
# opponent's graveyard from anywhere, instead exile it with a void counter on it") by turn 5, when the Arcanist attacks and
# casts the Bolt for free at Bot2. As it resolves Bot1 is asked which applies first and takes the Voidwalker's: the Bolt is
# exiled with a void counter, and the Arcanist's own no longer applies (CR 616.1f). On turn 6 Bot2 sacrifices the
# Voidwalker, which lets it play the one exiled card Bot1 owns with a void counter - proving the counter is there - and casts
# the Bolt at Bot1.

